\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.1}{\ignorespaces Basic variables sensitive to the interference between \Pqt  {}\Paqt  and single-top. \subref {fig:SR_Bulk_Final_l_4j_incl_blinded:ptl1} lepton \ensuremath  {p_{\text  {T}}}\xspace  distribution, \subref {fig:SR_Bulk_Final_l_4j_incl_blinded:etal1} lepton \ensuremath  {\storeEta }\xspace  distribution, \subref {fig:SR_Bulk_Final_l_4j_incl_blinded:ptb1} \( \ensuremath  {p_{\text  {T}}}\xspace  (b_{1}) \) distribution, \subref {fig:SR_Bulk_Final_l_4j_incl_blinded:ptb2} \( \ensuremath  {p_{\text  {T}}}\xspace  (b_{2}) \) distribution, \subref {fig:SR_Bulk_Final_l_4j_incl_blinded:pta1} \( \ensuremath  {p_{\text  {T}}}\xspace  (j_{1}) \) distribution, and \subref {fig:SR_Bulk_Final_l_4j_incl_blinded:pta2} \( \ensuremath  {p_{\text  {T}}}\xspace  (j_{2}) \) distribution. In the legend ``Exp'' indicates the prediction with data statistical uncertainty and ``Sys'' includes only MC statistical uncertainty as systematic uncertainty. The two predictions differ only in the modelling of the \ensuremath  {tW}\xspace  contribution and are marked DR (nominal sample) and DS.\spacefactor \@m {} The upper ratio panel displays the ratio of the \ensuremath  {tW}\xspace  contributions for each of the two modelling schemes to the combined \Pqt  {}\Paqt  +\ensuremath  {tW}\xspace  signal predictions. The lower ratio panel displays the ratio of each of the two predictions to the nominal one. Expected data uncertainty is displayed using error bars. Shaded areas show MC statistical uncertainty only. }}{46}{figure.caption.60}\protected@file@percent }
