\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.12}{\ignorespaces Improved \PW  selection. The \PW  boson is reconstructed from the leading jet (left), the hardest 2-jet combination (middle) or the combination of leading and subleading jet (right). More information on the plots is given in the caption of \cref  {fig:WhadReco_naive} and in the text. \subref {fig:WhadReco_1jpt_2} Reconstruct \ensuremath  {\PW  _\mathrm  {had}}\xspace  from the jet with highest \ensuremath  {p_{\text  {T}}}\xspace  , \subref {fig:WhadReco_2jpt_2} reconstruct from two jet combination with highest \ensuremath  {p_{\text  {T}}}\xspace  , \subref {fig:WhadReco_3jpt_2} reconstruct from the combination of leading and subleading jet, \subref {fig:WhadReco_1jpt_m} reconstruct from jet with highest \ensuremath  {p_{\text  {T}}}\xspace  including a cut on mass of the reconstructed \(\qty {60}{\ensuremath  {\text  {GeV}}\xspace  } < m(\ensuremath  {\PW  _\mathrm  {had}}\xspace  ) < \qty {100}{\ensuremath  {\text  {GeV}}\xspace  }\), \subref {fig:WhadReco_2jpt_m} reconstruct from two jet combination with highest \ensuremath  {p_{\text  {T}}}\xspace  including the same mass cut, \subref {fig:WhadReco_3jpt_m} reconstruct from leading and subleading jet including the same mass cut. }}{59}{figure.caption.72}\protected@file@percent }
